// The `typecheck` target's SECOND program, and only its second: `tsc` here
// judges the harness under `test/` and nothing else.
//
// The `.ts` files in `assembly/` and `examples/` are deliberately NOT in the
// program, and that is the whole point of this file's `include`. They are
// AssemblyScript — `i64`, `usize`, `heap.alloc`, `String.UTF8.decodeUnsafe` and
// `changetype` are its language, not TypeScript's, and `tsc` would report every
// one of them as an undefined name. The compiler that type-checks them is `asc`
// itself, run with `--noEmit`, which is the first half of the `typecheck`
// script in `./package.json`. Two compilers, two languages, one target — see
// `./README.md`'s first section for why this package holds both.
//
// It extends the root `tsconfig.base.json` for `module: nodenext`, which is
// what lets `test/golden.test.mjs` resolve the engine's own modules. The
// options on top are the ones `../lattice/tsconfig.json` argues in its own
// header, for the same reasons: nothing is emitted, the JSDoc is the program,
// and dependency `.d.ts` files are not this target's to fix.
{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "target": "es2022",
    "skipLibCheck": true
  },
  "include": ["test/**/*.mjs"]
}
